            <ArticleTitle>Effect of Physical Activity in Treatment of Paediatric Obesity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S57-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of the study was to compare the differences in anthropometric parameters, maximal oxygen uptake (VO₂max) and physical activity (PA) between groups of 146 obese boys and 128 obese girls. We tried to describe the relationships between changes in PA and changes in VO₂max, body fat, weight, waist circumference and hip circumference. We found statistically significant changes in VO₂max and waist circumference only in the group of boys and significant changes in VO₂max in the group of girls.</AbstractText>
